{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Establish a national standard for early bereavement signposting in the NHS",
        "additional_details": "No bereaved person should be left unaware of the help available simply because of their postcode, where a death occurs or which professional they encounter.\r\n\r\nBereavement can profoundly affect emotional, physical and mental wellbeing. Yet many people are left feeling isolated, overwhelmed and unsure where to turn. We believe clear, accessible bereavement information and signposting should be provided consistently across relevant NHS and care settings. Sustainable Government funding should support the national distribution and ongoing provision of these resources.",
        "background": "We urge the Government to ensure that every bereaved person using NHS services in England receives clear, compassionate, early signposting to tailored support.",
